WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.987
Try it.

2
00:00:00.987 --> 00:00:03.220
Lab 1 runs in PowerShell 7 on the kit's

3
00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.338
fictional certificate
inventory, with no tenant.

4
00:00:06.338 --> 00:00:09.780
Go to the kit's folder and make
this run's results folder,

5
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.922
named for the time you start, in U T C.

6
00:00:11.922 --> 00:00:13.988
Step one lists the certificates.

7
00:00:13.988 --> 00:00:17.348
Four of the five came from
the fictional enterprise C A,

8
00:00:17.348 --> 00:00:19.438
and two expire inside ninety days.

9
00:00:19.438 --> 00:00:24.556
The SQL P R D oh one T L S row matters
most: in seventy-two days every client that

10
00:00:24.556 --> 00:00:30.225
validates the certificate refuses to connect,
and Entra connections always validate.

11
00:00:30.225 --> 00:00:33.466
The SQL P R D oh two
login row expires sooner,

12
00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:36.962
in forty-one days, but
signing doesn't check expiry.

13
00:00:36.962 --> 00:00:39.274
The reason to replace it is its issuer.

14
00:00:39.274 --> 00:00:43.554
The last line counts the rows an
enterprise A D C S C A issued:

15
00:00:43.554 --> 00:00:48.120
four of five, each needing its
action before that C A is retired.
